  "question": "At Elephants by the Lake, which snake species were actually encountered in the September 2024 survey, how many other snake species are only older property records, and how many medically venomous species are documented? Please cite the exact source pages and do not turn a short non-detection into absence.",
  "elapsed_wall_s": 48.837,
  "status": "answer",
  "answer": "The user is asking about snake species encountered during the September 2024 survey at Elephants by the Lake, as well as the count of species only from older records and the number of medically venomous species documented. I have all this information in the available record.\n\nFrom the data:\n- **Encountered during survey (observed_during_survey)**: 3 species\n  1. Common Sand Boa (Eryx conicus) - Boidae - page 23\n  2. Striped Keelback (Amphiesma stolatum) - Colubridae - page 23\n  3. Barred Wolf Snake (Lycodon striatus) - Colubridae - page 23\n\n- **Only older property records (previous_property_record_not_observed_during_survey)**: 11 species\n  - Brahmini Blind Snake, Beaked Blind Snake, Rat Snake, Checkered Keelback, Olive Keelback, Common Wolf Snake, Russell's Wolf Snake, Spectacled Cobra, Russell's Viper, Saw-scaled Viper, Bamboo Pit Viper - pages 24\n\n- **Medically venomous species**: 4 species (all from older records, none encountered)\n  1. Spectacled Cobra (Naja naja) - Elapidae - page 24\n  2. Russell's Viper (Daboia russelli) - Viperidae - page 24\n  3. Saw-scaled",
